# The three response codes nothing else decodes.
#
# HAND BUILT FROM THE SPECIFICATION. The capture is a link coming up and every
# response in it is ACCEPT, so FATAL_ERROR, NON_FATAL_ERROR and NO_RESPONSE had
# never been decoded — and unlike the status bits, these three are not one code
# path. Each does something different to the rest of the phase.
#
# --- 1. NON_FATAL_ERROR on a shape that would otherwise carry a completion ---
#
# GET_PC's response is `ACCEPT HDR DATA STS CRC`. Answered with an error it is
# `NON_FATAL_ERROR STS CRC` — no header, no data. Figure 63, p.117, draws it,
# and the page states it in words: "The Response with Non-Fatal Error comprises
# a Response, a Status and a CRC. There is neither Header nor Data field during
# the Response phase."
#
# That sentence is the whole evidence for the OOB and flash shapes, which have
# no transaction figure of their own. Nothing decoded it until now.
#
# Getting it wrong is not cosmetic: the decoder would read three header bytes
# out of the status and CRC, and the CRC would land on nothing.
#
#   01     GET_PC
#   07     CRC
#
#   02     NON_FATAL_ERROR      Table 3, p.30. Reported as a warning.
#   0F 01  Status
#   12     CRC
#
# CRC bytes pasted from tools/crc_ref.py (rule R4).
CMD 01 07
TAR
RSP 02 0F 01 12

# --- 2. FATAL_ERROR, the same shape at a higher severity ---
#
# Figure 62, p.117, draws the identical response phase. The two codes differ
# only in what the decoder should say about them: "The eSPI target returns a
# Non-Fatal error in response to a command which is erroneous but does not
# impede the processing of the command and the forward progress of the bus"
# (p.117), where a fatal error does.
CMD 01 07
TAR
RSP 03 0F 01 79

# --- 3. NO_RESPONSE, where the phase simply is not driven ---
#
# The response byte is FFh and there is nothing after it. Not a truncated
# packet: the target never drove the phase at all, so there is no status and no
# CRC to read, and the fixture ends here on purpose.
#
# FFh shares its low nibble with WAIT_STATE's 1111b. Table 3 note 1, p.30, is
# what separates them — R1R0 is "always 00" except on NO_RESPONSE, where it is
# 11. A decoder that masks to the low nibble first classifies this as a wait
# state and then sits waiting for a response the specification says will never
# come.
CMD 25 FB
TAR
RSP FF
